**user**:
> How do I label the y-axis in plot_ly as percentages?
**assistant**:
> To label the y-axis as percentages in a `plotly` plot, you can use the `layout` function to modify the axis properties. Specifically, you'll set the `tickformat` of the `yaxis` to a percentage format. Here's how you can do it in R:
> 
> ```r
> library(plotly)
> 
> # Example data
> data <- data.frame(
>   x = c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5),
>   y = c(0.1, 0.15, 0.25, 0.3, 0.2)
> )
> 
> # Create a plotly plot
> plot <- plot_ly(data, x = ~x, y = ~y, type = 'scatter', mode = 'lines+markers') %>%
>   layout(
>     yaxis = list(
>       tickformat = "%",    # Format y-axis as percentages
>       title = "Y Axis (%)" # Optionally add a title to the y-axis
>     )
>   )
> 
> # Display the plot
> plot
> ```
> 
> In this example, `tickformat = "%"` tells `plotly` to display the y-axis values as percentages. Note that the actual values should be in decimal form (e.g., 0.1 for 10%) for this to work correctly. If you have any specific requirements or questions, feel free to ask!
